  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5110",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with RS4-11 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and other compounds. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for P2X purinoceptor 1 and Mollicellin N, both of which are themselves targets of palmarumycin CP18. This chain of targets leads to the final interaction with RS4-11, indicating a potential pathway where doxorubicin indirectly influences RS4-11 via these intermediaries. The shared involvement of palmarumycin CP18 as a common target in multiple paths strengthens the hypothesis that this compound plays a central role in linking doxorubicin to RS4-11. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of purinoceptor signaling in mediating the effects of doxorubicin on RS4-11, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
